237
00:19:03,302 --> 00:19:05,660
We should be getting
back to work. Stop that.

238
00:19:06,470 --> 00:19:09,458
But if you truly
don't belong to her,

239
00:19:09,542 --> 00:19:12,140
then you have the freedom
to do as you please, right?

240
00:19:12,620 --> 00:19:16,988
And so what if I do? You think
I would kiss you if I were

241
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:20,660
a human and not a fairy? Would
that change your tactic? What?

242
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:25,980
Why were shallow Miss
Bridget acting so close?

243
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,858
Would you have done
the same if you were trying

244
00:19:27,942 --> 00:19:30,828
to seduce Keith Powell
or Alf Hingley instead?

245
00:19:30,942 --> 00:19:34,110
I don't suppose so.
I would be too ashamed.

246
00:19:35,210 --> 00:19:39,038
But since I'm a fairy, it doesn't
embarrass you, is that it?

247
00:19:39,242 --> 00:19:42,698
Huh? It's no different than buying a
companion fairy at the market.

248
00:19:42,812 --> 00:19:45,488
It isn't like that.
If it is love you want,

249
00:19:45,572 --> 00:19:50,070
then you'll have to steal
my wing and command it of me.

250
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:57,000
There's something wrong. An.
Oh, no, I'm all right.

251
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:05,010
Huh? Let's go. Run with me!
Wait!

252
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:30,170
Uh,
goodness. What was that about?

253
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:33,038
It's time to start work.
And running is a quick

254
00:20:33,122 --> 00:20:35,060
way to put
your problems behind you.

255
00:20:36,380 --> 00:20:39,260
But I'll always be here
to listen if you want to talk.

256
00:20:40,220 --> 00:20:43,448
For now, focus on
making something amazing

257
00:20:43,532 --> 00:20:48,780
and competing against me.
All right. Sure. Mm.

